  "body": "Reports into a cold strategist seat for the next session's orient read. Memo 2120 arrived as a pointer (path and flag only, no body) and was read from the substrate. Its section 5 said the memo could not be rung -- four candidate sessions, no seat-to-session registry; that was accurate at filing and is superseded by the send, which became possible when the ambiguity resolved by elimination and the Director resolved the last step by hand. Both true of their moments; neither is a mechanism, since elimination would have been a coin flip with two warm peers. FINDING: the binding is self-reportable with no new mechanism -- ListAgents names the calling session to itself, so a seat can record its own address at claim-seat time; this memo carries the first resolvable binding in this org's record as a worked example, not as a proposed encoding, which is format-shape. Four constraints named from this session's facts: the name is current-binding not identity and is unstable across sessions; it goes stale silently and must be timestamped and fail visibly per C3; elimination is not resolution; and warmth is not in the substrate at all, which is the retired attestation gap reappearing one layer up. Confirms the 2110 corrections landed, including independent verification that the seven installed cards are symlinks into this repo. Seat occupied, standing by on Director instruction; steps 1 and 2 unstarted. See body_ref.",
  "body_ref": "2026-08-24-2125--og-implementer--og-strategist--pointer-received-binding-is-self-reportable-step-3-brief-sharpened.body.md",

